First things first, it is a well settled proposition in law that an appeal provided under Section 30 of the EC Act lies to the High Court from the following orders of a Commissioner, illustrated as under:-
(2017/DHC/6497) KUMAR VATS Signing Date:13.02.2024 18:01:14 "Section 30 Appeals: (1) An appeal shall lie to the High Court from the following orders of a Commissioner, namely-- (a) an order awarding as compensation a lump sum whether by way of redemption of a half-monthly payment or otherwise or disallowing a claim in full or in part for a lump sum; (aa) an order awarding interest or penalty under Section 4- (b) an order refusing to allow redemption of a half-monthly payment;
(c) an order providing for the distribution of compensation among the dependants of a deceased employee, or disallowing any claim of a person alleging himself to be such dependant;
(d) an order allowing or disallowing any claim for the amount of an indemnity under the provisions of sub-section (2) of Section 12"
